  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>The given position vectors can be written as</p><ul>\t<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>(</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>13</mn><mo>)</mo></math></li>\t<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi><mo>(</mo><mn>6</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>)</mo></math></li>\t<li><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>C</mi><mfenced><mrow><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfenced></math></li></ul><p>Also given that these three points are collinear.</p><p>Let us assume that the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>&nbsp;divides&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;in the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>k</mi><mo>:</mo><mn>1</mn></math>.</p><p>Since,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>B</mi><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>C</mi></math>&nbsp;are collinear&nbsp;</p><p><img src=\"assets\\st0074_d11a3c6990df.png\" style=\"width: 350px; height: 94px;\" /></p><p>On applying section&nbsp;formula for <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>z</mi></math>&nbsp;co-ordinate we get,</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>11</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>11</mn><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>13</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>19</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo></math>Ratio<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>:</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>19</mn></math></p><p>Now,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>19</mn><mo>+</mo><mfenced><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac><mn>9</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfenced><mo>&#215;</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>6</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>19</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>117</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>117</mn><mn>19</mn></mfrac></math></p><p>Now similarly,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>190</mn></mrow><mn>21</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>11</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>&#946;</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>41</mn><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8756;</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>19</mn><mi>&#945;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>&#946;</mi></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mfenced><mrow><mn>117</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>123</mn></mrow></mfenced><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>36</mn></math></p><p>Hence this is the correct option.</p></blockquote>"
  }
